      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 47-year-old African American man was seen for routine follow-up for his human immunodeficiency virus (HIV). The patient's medical history included insomnia, gastroesophageal reflux disease, pulmonary embolism, right shoulder musculoskeletal pain, latent tuberculosis infection, sickle cell trait (hemoglobin S variant), and HIV of 24 years' duration."},
